# Owner scope (housekeeping)

This toolkit manages hygiene for **one** GitHub user/org: `config.toml` `owner`
(or `--owner`). It is not a network-wide suggestion or spam tool.

## Defaults (keep when forking)

- Scan, triage, comment, and open fix PRs **only** under that `owner`.
- Authenticate `gh` as the operator who owns or administers those repos.
- Never mass-open issues/PRs or drive-by comments on unrelated public repos.
- `--repos` may narrow to a subset of the owner’s repos; it must not expand
  outside `owner`.
- If this repository is forked for reuse, set the fork’s own `owner` and stay
  inside that boundary. Forkers may rewrite these rules, but the shipped sane
  default is owner-scoped only.

See `AGENTS.md` § Owner scope and `.cursor/skills/housekeeping/SKILL.md`.
